<title>SENEGAL: Senegal river energy plan gets islamic bank funds.</title>
<headline>Senegal river energy plan gets islamic bank funds.</headline>
<dateline>DAKAR 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Islamic Development Bank (IDB) funds totalling  12 billion CFA francs have been granted for a West African river energy  project including Mali, Mauritania and Senegal, a Senegal government  minister said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are happy to state that the IDB's contribution covers 33 percent  of the needed finances,&quot; said Minister of Finance Papa Ousmane Sacko,  whose country hosts the headquarters of the Organisation for the Development  of River Senegal (OMVS).</p>
<p>The funds, along with other contributions would be used for the building  of a hydro-electric dam from September due for completion in 2000,  Organisation officials said.</p>
<p>Energy would be divided as follows: Mali 52 percent, Senegal 33 percent  and Mauritania 15 percent, they said.</p>
<p>($=620 CFA)</p>
<p>-- Abidjan newsroom, + 225 21 90 90</p>
</text>
